1
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:05,197
This love in my heart,
it will burn on forever!

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:09,037
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop!

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,177
No matter where you
are, nothing is too far!

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:15,857
With our everlasting bones,
we'll reach it, we are home!

5
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:22,637
I'm

6
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:23,917
so truly grateful!

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,800
I ran into you on that day so long ago!

8
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,397
We laughed every moment
with tears in our eyes!

9
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,880
Till we knew we weren't alone!

10
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:41,820
The blowing wind came in
and joined us on our way!

11
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:47,097
And with it I know we'll rise!

12
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:49,797
We'll be flying up high!

13
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,920
Why, tell me why are you giving up?

14
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:56,160
Why, tell me why you want to fight alone?

15
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:59,620
Hey, what kind of future
do you think you have?

16
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:03,197
Your dream is already in your hands.

17
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:06,937
This love in my heart,
it will burn off forever.

18
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:10,757
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop.

19
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,897
I don't matter where you
are, nothing is too far.

20
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:16,457
With our everlasting
plans, we'll reach it.

21
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:20,517
We are home from the horizon,
out on the edge of the world.

22
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,497
If there is a place that
I'd want to take you to?

23
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:24,897
Let's head for it then!

24
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:28,457
But as for the way, we already know.

25
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:31,500
We promised it long ago.

26
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:45,317
You scream by your voice.

27
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,237
That can't break through the silence?

28
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:48,817
Feeling defeated.

29
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,037
It crushes your helpless heart.

30
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,697
I've got your back, I swear.

31
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:54,177
I'll always be here.

32
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:57,960
Let's put our fate within
this light under the sun.

33
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:02,880
Can you close your eyes and
just listen to my voice?

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,897
Let's find the answer together.

35
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,577
I'm telling you in our path.

36
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:09,617
I trust that it will lead us.

37
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,517
To another sea untarded.

38
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,417
Cause now we are home.

39
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:16,197
On the horizon, out on
the edge of the world.

40
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:19,217
There is a place I want to take you to.

41
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:20,697
Let's head for it then.

42
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:24,340
But as for the way we already know.

43
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:27,260
We promised it long ago.

44
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:31,760
Are you really gonna wait here?

45
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:34,607
We're right in the middle
of enemy territory.

46
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,780
Oh, wait!

47
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,640
Remember what Pound said?

48
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:44,040
About the last person who
took out a sweet general?

49
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:48,917
Big Mom summoned a storm along
with an army hungry for revenge.

50
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,537
and their target didn't survive an instant
so we know that the enemy will come,

51
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:57,557
but Sanji on the other
hand, Sanji will be back!

52
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:00,840
I'll wait just like I said.

53
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:11,840
Chess look at mine, handsome foliage,
it's been ruined, chopped down.

54
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:24,677
What's going on?

55
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:27,117
It was clear only a second ago.

56
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:29,259
Where are those clouds coming from?

57
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:33,297
kingbaum, what's causing all this?

58
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:37,757
It's coming from the whole
cake Shit where mama lives.

59
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,500
Her fury is tremendous.

60
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:43,580
Then those clouds—are

61
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:45,830
hers?

62
00:03:45,913 --> 00:03:46,743
No

63
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:49,090
way!

64
00:03:49,173 --> 00:03:50,003
All

65
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:53,880
that power—coming from

66
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:55,697
one person!

67
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:56,610
My climate

68
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,957
tax can't hold a candle
to something like that.

69
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:00,870
Linlin can

70
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:06,317
command the weather quite literally.

71
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,360
quite literally

72
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:13,432
Once her rage is awakened, there's
nothing in this world that can stop her!

73
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:37,500
Zeus and Prometheus are
running wild up there!

74
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:42,360
Mama's mad.

75
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:44,480
I'm really mad.

76
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:38,780
Clear the way!

77
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:41,060
The forces of fury are marching!

78
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,217
They're off to avenge General Cracker.

79
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,130
Make way!

80
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:46,900
Move it, you idiots!

81
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:00,840
Ha ha ha!

82
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,060
A whole army!

83
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,637
They're hunting down Straw Hat, no doubt.

84
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:06,485
The rat's as good as dead now.

85
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,980
Wow, that's funny.

86
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:16,514
He won't run because he's
waiting for his old pal Sanji.

87
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:20,200
Good thing you said your goodbyes.

88
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,720
Aw, damn!

89
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:26,760
That's Bobbin the Disposer!

90
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:30,120
Amand the Mademoiselle!

91
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:33,700
And Mondor the Scribe!

92
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:36,707
Wonder how much all
those bounties add up to.

93
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:51,438
I'm staying right here and
I'm not moving on a hitch!

94
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:57,180
Who am I kidding?

95
00:06:57,540 --> 00:06:59,697
Even Straw Hat wouldn't
be stupid enough to

96
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:02,427
sit around after getting
a load of that army.

97
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:27,960
It's raining.

98
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,997
This is...

99
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,920
syrup, I think.

100
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,837
Uh, what's wrong?

101
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:42,420
I won't eat syrup or anything,

102
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:46,000
not unless Sanji's the one cooking it.

103
00:07:58,340 --> 00:07:59,660
Mama's here!

104
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:07,657
Are you being good, boys and girls?

105
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:09,580
Mama, I've got a problem.

106
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:11,640
What is it, Inanna?

107
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:15,177
The head chef's being mean
and won't let me use a knife.

108
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:17,320
I just wanna cut open my dolly.

109
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,380
That won't do at all, will it?

110
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:23,560
Hey, Dials and Dragé,
go and get her a knife.

111
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,560
No way, no how, Mama.

112
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:29,017
She says she wants to cut her dolly,
but she's gonna pop our balloon.

113
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:32,637
Yeah, she's a bad girl, and I'm
gonna kill her someday for sure.

114
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:33,917
Mama, kill her first.

115
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,777
We shouldn't say mean things like
that to each other, should we, Mama?

116
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:39,377
Ha ha ha ha!

117
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:40,900
It's only natural.

118
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:44,497
Everyone has a couple hundred
people that they want dead.

119
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:47,860
But let's hold off on the
killing for now, all right?

120
00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:51,867
Your big sister pudding is getting
married tomorrow, you know?

121
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:53,158
Aren't you excited?

122
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:59,720
We'll have a delicious wedding
cake, big enough for everyone.

123
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,020
Hooray! Hooray! Yay!

124
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,477
Now, this should be fun.

125
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:08,440
I'm going to meet the
Groob's family. D 'or!

126
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:15,860
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

127
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:18,040
Ma, ma, ma, ma, ma.

128
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:21,949
It's truly a pleasure to have
you here, Jeremiah Double Six.

129
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,720
Sorry if I'm late.

130
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:25,840
So that's Big Mom.

131
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:29,560
I had a little hiccup to take care of.

132
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:31,862
Everything should be peachy now.

133
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:43,740
Oh, Pudding!

134
00:09:44,060 --> 00:09:44,940
There you are!

135
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:46,380
Pardon the delay.

136
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:56,360
You know, I've heard so
much about Sanji already.

137
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:58,878
What a coincidence that he's a chef.

138
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:01,752
Why, he's a perfect match for my Pudding.

139
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:05,717
Well, they're getting married
either way, so it doesn't matter.

140
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:08,300
This is strictly a political arrangement.

141
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:14,260
But it's lovely that we can find something
that works to our mutual benefit, Judge.

142
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:18,010
Indeed.

143
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:22,931
Though it would make me even happier
if our children could share in the joy.

144
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:27,660
Let's give them a perfect wedding.

145
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,980
A toast to their future.

146
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:54,580
Black tea, green tea, choose please!

147
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:57,820
Uh, black? Yeah!

148
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:11,097
Take a bite, also nice!

149
00:11:11,180 --> 00:11:12,457
Liza, please start with me!

150
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:13,777
Take a bite, also nice!

151
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:15,077
Liza, won't you start with me?

152
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:18,097
I know just a thing you need,
have a bit of sweet, honey!

153
00:11:18,180 --> 00:11:20,580
It's very sweet!

154
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:38,620
I usually don't hate food but I hate you.

155
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:50,317
Noisiest damn food I've ever seen.

156
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:54,520
You, don't it taste so yummy?

157
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:05,100
Um, Sanji.

158
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:55,540
We are kaput.

159
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:57,580
We are Gatling, I say.

160
00:12:58,740 --> 00:12:59,760
No way.

161
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:01,220
There's too many.

162
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:19,750
Luffy.

163
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:31,217
Come on, please, you just need to get
out of here and hide for a little while.

164
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:32,757
You can come back later!

165
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,317
You're not breaking your word,

166
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:38,857
I won't go—what happens if Saji
comes back here while I'm gone?

167
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:42,377
It's okay, leave this fight to me, Lupi.

168
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:45,537
This is impossible—we're in the
middle of an emperor's territory.

169
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:46,820
emperor's territory

170
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,420
It's an entire army!

171
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:14,288
There's no way you can win!

172
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:19,020
Shawhead Nico is now in sight!

173
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:28,220
I told him I would be here!

174
00:14:32,060 --> 00:14:34,120
I won't break my promise!

175
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:43,640
You led my friends to this island?

176
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:44,960
I'm sorry.

177
00:14:47,060 --> 00:14:49,877
I gave Luffy my word that I
would bring you to the southwest

178
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:53,197
coast so you would be able
to get away from Mama safely.

179
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:57,221
But I couldn't make it happen, and
now they're all in grave danger.

180
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:58,760
I see now.

181
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:03,613
I wondered how they managed to pass
through all that security to get here.

182
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,557
It was thanks to you.

183
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:07,040
I know you meant well.

184
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:12,621
That said, no matter what, I still
wouldn't have gone to the coast.

185
00:15:13,860 --> 00:15:17,017
If you're worried about the invitation,
you can let me take the blame.

186
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:17,930
She's my mom.

187
00:15:18,013 --> 00:15:18,843
I'll be fine.

188
00:15:18,926 --> 00:15:20,637
Just don't show up at the ceremony.

189
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:23,277
She's used to arranged marriages,

190
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:26,877
so she puts special bracelets on people
who seem like they might run away.

191
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:31,077
If you try to leave the island
with one, I know it explodes.

192
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:37,257
Your mom has the key to unlock this thing.

193
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:41,717
If I want to get it, then I have
to defeat the big mom pirates.

194
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:45,037
So she's already gotten to you sadly.

195
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:49,697
Yeah, she's thinking ahead, and
even if that weren't the case,

196
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:55,337
no one here has my back,

197
00:15:55,420 --> 00:16:02,420
even

198
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:05,550
though

199
00:16:05,633 --> 00:16:06,463
we're brothers.

200
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:13,320
They still did this.

201
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:17,660
Your own family beat you that badly?

202
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:19,200
That's right.

203
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:20,910
But why?

204
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:27,340
Because to them, I'm just a failure
who shouldn't be allowed to live.

205
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:33,700
I've never once been happy
about being born as royalty.

206
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:40,100
That's the reason I went out to sea.

207
00:16:41,820 --> 00:16:44,820
Searching for a place I
wasn't even sure was real.

208
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:47,400
And now,

209
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:52,500
if I try to prevent
this arranged marriage,

210
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:57,480
they'll slaughter all my friends and me.

211
00:16:58,260 --> 00:17:03,500
On top of that, they're going to kill the
man in the East Blue who saved my life.

212
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:06,400
The man who I respect as my real father.

213
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:10,000
No matter what I do at this
point, there's no way out.

214
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:16,700
Which is why I've decided that
I won't fight this anymore.

215
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:25,318
I'm willing to accept this
marriage on one condition.

216
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:28,500
I want Big Mom to let
my friends go unharmed.

217
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:36,300
Our soldiers are out there
attacking as we speak.

218
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:39,720
I'm so sorry.

219
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:41,657
You're in such pain,

220
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:47,717
and it's all because of what I did,
pudding—it's not your fault. I promise.

221
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:48,630
13

222
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:53,877
years ago,

223
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:59,837
I managed to escape hell only
to walk right back in again.

224
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:00,750
But

225
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:06,037
I should try to be happy after all—I
was free for all of these years, right?

226
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:06,950
The friends

227
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:10,080
who helped me improve as a chef, and the

228
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:12,857
companions who joined me in my travels.

229
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:13,770
I'm grateful

230
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:17,157
to all of the people I met out there.

231
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,070
And I

232
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:21,017
can't bear to hurt them.

233
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:21,930
That's why

234
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:26,057
my adventure ends here.

235
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:26,970
Hey, don't

236
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:33,890
cry!

237
00:18:33,973 --> 00:18:35,217
It makes me feel worse.

238
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:36,130
feel worse

239
00:18:36,900 --> 00:18:37,841
Look, it's okay.

240
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:41,380
But listen.

241
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:43,590
Sanji.

242
00:18:44,780 --> 00:18:45,920
I promise.

243
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:51,240
If you decide to marry me,
I won't let it be hell.

244
00:18:59,820 --> 00:19:01,560
Oh dear, what am I saying?

245
00:19:01,820 --> 00:19:05,349
You're suffering so much and
I'm making everything about me.

246
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:09,797
You don't want to marry me, so of
course this would be hell for you.

247
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:12,697
Why am I being so insensitive
at a time like this?

248
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:18,137
It's awful, I'm so embarrassed after
all you and I have only just met,

249
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:23,077
so how could I possibly hope to fill the
hole in your heart, and besides all that.

250
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:27,200
You still might change your mind,
so I was being presumptuous, too.

251
00:19:58,680 --> 00:20:01,237
You're my salvation.

252
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:04,480
What are you saying?

253
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:09,260
Pudding, if you'll have me.

254
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:14,400
I want us to get married tomorrow.

255
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,320
Hey, what gives?

256
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:31,400
Get down here!

257
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:36,150
Stop!

258
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:46,331
You don't look like anything special,
so I wasn't expecting power like that.

259
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:49,618
I suppose I should have paid
better attention to you.

